1
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:04,690
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:10,530
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:14,390
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:17,200
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:21,270
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:27,530
I want you to join us, Guts!

7
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:32,200
Acting so friendly after you stabbed me...

8
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,160
What do you want?

9
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:40,110
To settle this with our swords...

10
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,680
All right...

11
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:49,690
I rather enjoy settling things by force...

12
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:50,890
Griffith!

13
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:54,610
No matter what, I will have what I want.

14
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:58,520
I've had enough of you acting so stuck up...

15
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,180
It makes me sick!

16
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,520
Feel no shame about shape

17
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:33,440
Weather changes their phrase

18
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:37,200
Even mother will show you another way

19
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,570
So put your glasses on

20
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:41,660
Nothing will be wrong

21
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:43,870
There's no blame. There's no fame

22
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,700
It's up to you

23
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:49,330
The first words should be found

24
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:52,960
Whatever holds you back

25
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,340
I...

26
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:55,460
...can...

27
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:57,630
I can get it off

28
00:01:57,630 --> 00:01:58,630
Tell me what...

29
00:01:58,630 --> 00:01:59,640
Tell me what...

30
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,470
Tell me what you want

31
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:02,560
I don't know why...

32
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,560
Don't know why...

33
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,560
Don't know why you're afraid

34
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:06,730
Tell me what...

35
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:07,690
Tell me what...

36
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:09,350
Tell me what you'd say

37
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,690
I don't know why...

38
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:11,770
Don't know why...

39
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:12,570
Too late...

40
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:14,190
It's too late

41
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:23,120
First Battle

42
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,370
Griffith!

43
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:47,560
He's something else...

44
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:52,270
I bet I could split steel with this sword...

45
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:54,610
...but he easily evades each blow...

46
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:57,990
...and just uses one arm
to handle his narrow blade!

47
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:01,280
He's a great fighter!

48
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:08,830
I could suspend this duel until you've
recovered completely, if you like.

49
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:09,750
Shut up!

50
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,000
I'll win!

51
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,960
I'll definitely beat him!

52
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,800
Faster!

53
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,300
Stronger!

54
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:28,930
The kid is challenging Griffith again.
He didn't learn his lesson at all!

55
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,850
Kill him!

56
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:32,270
Corkus, stop it!

57
00:03:32,770 --> 00:03:33,650
What?

58
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:35,150
It's Griffith's orders!

59
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:36,480
You must not bother them!

60
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,820
I will take this opportunity to kill him.

61
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:38,360
Move!

62
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:43,030
When did you become leader, Corkus?

63
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:46,870
Griffith's orders are absolute.

64
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:09,890
I've got him!

65
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:23,780
It's settled...

66
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:26,660
I like the way you fight.

67
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,240
You'll go to any length
to defeat your opponent.

68
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,200
However, you can't wield
your sword unless I move.

69
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:33,710
What do you say?

70
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,580
I wouldn't mind if you'd rather we desist.

71
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:40,170
You talk too much. It's annoying.

72
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,920
Let me tell you something.

73
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,130
In a battle, your mouth...

74
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,180
...is to be used like this!

75
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:03,820
Griffith!

76
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:20,290
I've never seen Griffith
knocked to the ground like that!

77
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,840
Do you like the taste of your own blood?

78
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:29,470
I bet you've never had
that fancy face beaten in!

79
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,110
He did it!

80
00:05:40,610 --> 00:05:42,690
You struck me quite soundly...

81
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,110
But this is the end.

82
00:05:45,110 --> 00:05:49,870
Admit defeat amenably
or have your shoulder joint dislocated.

83
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,370
It doesn't matter to me...

84
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,500
You bastard...

85
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:08,220
Way to go!

86
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,640
That's our Griffith!

87
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,850
Yeah, that's Griffith for you!

88
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:18,440
You really are the best.

89
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,940
You loser!

90
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:24,360
You look pathetic, have you lost your nerve?

91
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:27,400
Griffith?

92
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,240
Now...

93
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,700
...you are mine.

94
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,750
Do you mean it?

95
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:45,170
He is a member of ours from now on!

96
00:06:45,170 --> 00:06:47,840
Yeah!

97
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:55,350
It's so strange...

98
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:02,520
Griffith has never,
ever said such kind words...

99
00:07:03,650 --> 00:07:04,900
...to anyone!

100
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:28,050
They've been nicknamed
the Grim Reapers of the Battlefield...

101
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:30,630
...since they're
seemingly invincible in battle.

102
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:33,390
We do not need to worry
ourselves about them...

103
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:35,930
...since they are
a subsidiary of the Midland army.

104
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,560
Besides, mercenaries
are merely cannon fodder.

105
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:44,230
But what if they gain power
and earn the king's trust?

106
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:47,570
We would face the loss of
our prestige, honor, and pride.

107
00:07:47,570 --> 00:07:48,690
Indeed...

108
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,950
This is irritating!

109
00:07:57,490 --> 00:07:58,740
I was beaten...

110
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,370
...completely!

111
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:01,710
It's almost a joke!

112
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:03,620
He...

113
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:06,040
...talks openly, and smiles
like some innocent kid...

114
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:07,920
But...

115
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:12,010
...he dislocated my shoulder
joint cleanly, without hesitation...

116
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:15,050
...just like plucking off a doll's arm...

117
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,640
Damn it!

118
00:08:20,970 --> 00:08:22,770
Who the hell is he?

119
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,860
Are you serious about killing him, Corkus?

120
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:27,650
Sheesh!

121
00:08:27,650 --> 00:08:29,570
Don't chicken out at the last moment.

122
00:08:29,570 --> 00:08:30,900
There are seven of us!

123
00:08:31,610 --> 00:08:34,200
You said you didn't like him either, right?

124
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,110
Don't forget he killed Dan.

125
00:08:36,110 --> 00:08:38,660
But he's so strong and skilled.

126
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:39,870
On top of that, Griffith...

127
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,750
Don't worry.

128
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,660
We'll catch him off guard.

129
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:46,580
Plus, he's injured and
can't possibly lift his sword.

130
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:50,670
We'll convince Griffith that the kid escaped...

131
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:53,260
...after we dump his body in the woods.

132
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:56,760
This bunch will be no problem compared to him...

133
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:59,100
Sam, you go first!

134
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,180
Again?

135
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,640
You never go first.

136
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,930
You better not do it.

137
00:09:03,230 --> 00:09:04,600
C-Casca.

138
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:08,190
He is still far beyond your skill, even injured.

139
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:11,020
I'll see about that.

140
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:13,240
Go back to your tent like a good boy, Corkus.

141
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,570
Casca, why are you trying to save him?

142
00:09:16,070 --> 00:09:17,820
Oh, I see.

143
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:19,580
You lay together for two nights...

144
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,910
No wonder you have some feelings for him...

145
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:24,500
If you say anything like that ever again...

146
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,080
...I'll chop your head off.

147
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,420
J-Just kidding...

148
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:28,380
I'm kidding.

149
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:34,510
Let's go.

150
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,270
It looks like I owe you two...

151
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:54,110
I should thank you at least.

152
00:09:54,110 --> 00:09:55,690
You're mistaken...

153
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:57,860
I just acted on Griffith's orders.

154
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,870
Otherwise, I don't give a damn about you.

155
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:05,500
I hope you drop dead
in battle as soon as you can.

156
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,920
Our foes' base is on the hill
and manned by 2,000 soldiers.

157
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:55,840
Our job is to burn the provisions and
other supplies stored behind the hill.

158
00:10:56,760 --> 00:11:00,970
Theoretically, they'll fortify the front
of the hill in case of night attacks.

159
00:11:01,590 --> 00:11:02,800
So we...

160
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:06,850
...will detour along the river and
attempt a surprise attack on their rear.

161
00:11:07,270 --> 00:11:11,230
When we accomplish our goal,
we'll take the shortest route back...

162
00:11:11,230 --> 00:11:14,560
...right through the midst of their forces.

163
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:16,400
Through the enemy?

164
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:18,030
Any backup?

165
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:18,900
None.

166
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:22,700
It seems they can't afford
to send units for a night attack.

167
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:24,950
They're just a bunch of cowards.

168
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,710
The rear guard will be...

169
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,370
Guts...

170
00:11:32,370 --> 00:11:33,580
I want you to do it.

171
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,130
You'll help your fellow soldiers escape...

172
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:43,180
...holding off hundreds of cavalrymen...

173
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:45,300
...on a straight road in the woods.

174
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:46,890
Can you manage?

175
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:48,220
It's an order, isn't it?

176
00:11:49,270 --> 00:11:50,430
It is.

177
00:11:50,430 --> 00:11:52,560
Griffith is trying to put
the kid's skill to the test.

178
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:55,310
Poor guy, I doubt he'll
make it through in one piece.

179
00:11:55,310 --> 00:11:56,940
He might try to sneak away.

180
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:57,570
That's not it!

181
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:02,490
Griffith wouldn't give him such
an important job just as a test...

182
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:05,570
Griffith truly counts on him.

183
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:11,370
Now I don't even have to bother killing him.

184
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:43,530
We're marching in the river, not going along it.

185
00:12:44,610 --> 00:12:46,320
Either way, the enemy won't predict...

186
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:49,530
...us making a surprise attack
by traveling up such a rapid stream.

187
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:52,080
In addition, this gale...

188
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:54,460
...will drown out the noise of our march.

189
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:56,290
Then we'll set the fire windward...

190
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:58,540
...when we attack from behind.

191
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:02,460
Everything's been calculated, huh...

192
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,090
It's freezing.

193
00:13:40,090 --> 00:13:42,500
Lookout duty on such a creepy night...

194
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:47,880
Unlike us, even wolves wouldn't go out tonight.

195
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:03,650
T-The enemy?

196
00:14:06,150 --> 00:14:08,410
W-Why are they coming from that direction?

197
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:14,830
E-Enemy raid!

198
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:16,910
An enemy raid?

199
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:25,420
Set the fires!

200
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,470
They set fire to the gunpowder!

201
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:42,560
Don't stop to play with them!

202
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:43,940
Break through in a single rush!

203
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,240
Move double file!

204
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:54,990
Clear out!

205
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:00,620
General!

206
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:04,750
The gale is fanning
the flames towards the base!

207
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:05,710
Damn!

208
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:07,630
Take the heavy cavalry to the front!

209
00:15:08,590 --> 00:15:11,510
Allowing our base to be
destroyed by mere mercenaries...

210
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:13,260
...is a disgrace to us knights!

211
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:18,480
It's amazing!

212
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:21,480
I have never been part of
such an efficient raid before...

213
00:15:27,110 --> 00:15:29,150
Now it's my job to take care of the rest!

214
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:42,790
Get out of here!

215
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,130
I-I will!

216
00:15:46,460 --> 00:15:47,340
Follow me...

217
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,170
Come on, keep up!

218
00:15:57,510 --> 00:15:59,850
Good job, Griffith.

219
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:02,190
They will probably
be stalled for at least a month...

220
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,150
I still have my duties to complete.

221
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:10,070
Excuse me.

222
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:10,900
Hey!

223
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:12,450
What an insolent attitude!

224
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,580
How much is the damage?

225
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:20,910
No big deal.

226
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:21,540
I see.

227
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:23,790
It's thanks to how well
our rear guard held out...

228
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:26,880
...the enemy could hardly get close to us.

229
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:29,340
He handled a group of
heavy cavalrymen all by himself...

230
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:31,550
...even though it was on
a straight road in the woods.

231
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:33,340
He really is something.

232
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:35,970
Rickert!

233
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:37,220
Where is Guts?

234
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:38,470
He sent me on ahead.

235
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:41,430
I hope he's still alive.

236
00:17:03,410 --> 00:17:05,120
It's time for me to go back...

237
00:17:10,090 --> 00:17:11,210
Damn it!

238
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:19,800
I screwed up...

239
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:28,230
Griffith!

240
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,230
Grab my hand!

241
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:36,950
Retreat!

242
00:17:36,950 --> 00:17:38,070
D-Don't let them get away!

243
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,870
Why did you come back here?

244
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:42,700
Don't talk!

245
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:43,790
You'll bite your tongue!

246
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:51,590
This is no good!

247
00:17:51,590 --> 00:17:53,130
They'll catch us because
we're double mounted!

248
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,090
Hang on!

249
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:58,680
We're almost to the edge of the woods!

250
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:02,060
Ready!

251
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:03,560
Disperse!

252
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:04,810
What?

253
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,520
Fire!

254
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,410
R-Retreat!

255
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:24,410
Retreat!

256
00:18:50,690 --> 00:18:54,230
At any rate, it was
amazing the way Guts fought.

257
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:57,320
Just as Griffith expected,
he has what it takes.

258
00:18:58,610 --> 00:19:01,660
By the way, Guts is nowhere to be found.

259
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,460
Despite his age...

260
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,670
...Griffith has the qualities of a great leader...

261
00:19:13,670 --> 00:19:15,170
...and the others rely on him completely.

262
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:18,050
Besides that, he's got perfect judgment...

263
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:19,920
...and he knows how to take decisive action...

264
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,390
He's more than just
the leader of a mercenary band...

265
00:19:24,390 --> 00:19:25,720
Mr. Guts...

266
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:26,850
What are you doing?

267
00:19:26,850 --> 00:19:28,600
Are you cooling off up here?

268
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:30,730
Thanks for your help before.

269
00:19:30,730 --> 00:19:32,650
I narrowly escaped because of you.

270
00:19:32,650 --> 00:19:34,440
I'm Rickert.

271
00:19:34,770 --> 00:19:36,520
I really admire you.

272
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,230
I have never seen anyone who is...

273
00:19:38,230 --> 00:19:40,570
...such an amazing fighter,
except for Mr. Griffith.

274
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,780
I have done nothing but my duty.

275
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,370
I have no reason to be thanked.

276
00:19:46,870 --> 00:19:48,580
The same thing goes for you.

277
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,710
Well, I'm not going
to argue with you about it.

278
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,670
Anyway, come with us.

279
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,540
A party isn't as lively without the hero.

280
00:19:56,500 --> 00:20:00,510
A feast is being held, partly as a welcome.

281
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:02,970
I-I never asked for anything like that!

282
00:20:07,390 --> 00:20:08,810
W-What are you doing?

283
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:12,770
Don't touch me!

284
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:16,980
Don't be shy.

285
00:20:18,110 --> 00:20:19,440
L-Let go of me!

286
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,660
Hey, here he comes.

287
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:30,660
P-Put me down, you big-headed bastard!

288
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:31,790
I am Pippin.

289
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:35,290
Y-You.

290
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,460
Drink.

291
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:38,710
Everyone!

292
00:20:38,710 --> 00:20:41,670
Let's drink in celebration
of our brash, new friend!

293
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,360
I give you real credit, rookie!

294
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:59,520
You're pretty impressive!

295
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:03,360
You cut off the enemy's attack all
by yourself, even when outnumbered!

296
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,910
As Griffith thought, you have what it takes!

297
00:21:05,910 --> 00:21:09,330
Sure, you've got some issues,
but it's good to have you on board!

298
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,290
Let's kick back, rookie!

299
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:25,430
That bastard...

300
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:05,800
Looking back, the morning comes.

301
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:09,300
Don't find your face in your glass.

302
00:22:10,350 --> 00:22:13,430
Take the moonlight by the tail.

303
00:22:13,430 --> 00:22:16,390
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

304
00:22:17,850 --> 00:22:19,600
What is that?

305
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,860
It's just the same.

306
00:22:20,860 --> 00:22:24,030
What is trying your crown?

307
00:22:25,110 --> 00:22:28,320
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

308
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:31,370
So wear my glass. You're fading.

309
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:51,260
I'm waiting so long.

310
00:22:51,260 --> 00:23:00,350
I'm waiting...

